Found while fixing k146. f9f2139 (k144), 73f0f26 (k142) and 7e71bb1 (k145) were built in `.claude/worktrees/<name>` checkouts without their own `npm ci`: Node resolved nunjucks from the main checkout's `node_modules`, and esbuild wrote `../../../node_modules/...` paths into `dist/skilletor.js`. `check-dist` in the same worktree resolved the same way and passed locally; CI (own `node_modules`) failed.

## Proposal

`scripts/esbuild.config.mjs` (and so `check-dist`) refuses to build when nunjucks or esbuild resolve from outside the repo's own `node_modules`, and says to run `npm ci`.

## Done when

A build in a worktree without `node_modules` fails locally with that message, the same way CI would; a normal build is unchanged; a test covers it.

